schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Token allowances (dApp spending permissions)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The permission a user grants a smart contract to access/spend their
    tokens when using a dApp; the article's core security advice is to limit
    the allowance to the immediate trade size rather than the full balance.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Presented as a "Security Essentials" item in creating-buying-earning.md,
    alongside seed-phrase custody and starting-small advice.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - seed-phrase-custody (the other named security essential in the same article)
  important_distinctions:
    - "an allowance is a revocable smart-contract permission, distinct from a seed phrase, which is full wallet control"
  tensions:
    - convenience-of-unlimited-approval vs exposure-if-that-contract-is-later-exploited
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    The article gives the rule ("limit allowances") without explaining how to
    check or revoke existing allowances (e.g. via a token-approval checker
    tool) — a practical gap for a true beginner guide.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/creating-buying-earning.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-a7cccf043614
  source_lineage: creating-buying-earning.md
